# ── Type: ContextScope ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scope is "the context within which an assertion holds." The same claim can be
# verified in one scope and fictional in another. The substrate registers only
# the type and the universal physical_reality scope; PAI-system scopes are in
# scopes.nq. Add your own scopes by extending scopes.nq.
</epistemology/context_scope> </type/object/type> </type/type> .
</epistemology/context_scope> </type/object/name> "ContextScope" .
</epistemology/context_scope> </common/topic/description> "The context within which an assertion holds. Substrate: physical_reality. PAI scopes in scopes.nq." .

</epistemology/scope/physical_reality> </type/object/type> </epistemology/context_scope> .
</epistemology/scope/physical_reality> </type/object/name> "physical_reality" .
</epistemology/scope/physical_reality> </common/topic/description> "Claims that hold in the world, independent of any narrative or system layer." .

